      "text_raw": "More interpolation, to save\nmore amplifiers and to fur-\nther reduce the input capa-\ncitance, increases the\ncapacitance C at the\nmirror\ninner node of the current\nmirrors. As a result, the\nmaximum frequency at\nwhich the interpolation can\nbe carried out decreases.\nAn example is given in\nthis slide of the node capaci-\ntance and resulting −3 dB\nfrequency for an interpola-\ntor realized in 0.5 mm\nCMOS.\nA compromise is to be\ntaken.",
      "text": "More interpolation, to save more amplifiers and to further reduce the input capacitance, increases the capacitance C at the mirror inner node of the current mirrors. As a result, the maximum frequency at which the interpolation can be carried out decreases. An example is given in this slide of the node capacitance and resulting −3 dB frequency for an interpolator realized in 0.5 mm CMOS. A compromise is to be taken."
    }
